Print unified diffs in-process on wasip1 instead of running `diff -u`.

Reason: buf's diff package writes both sides to temp files and runs the
external `diff -u` binary. wasip1 cannot start processes, so `buf format -d`
and `-w` (and config migrate, source edit) fail with `exec: "diff":
executable file not found in $PATH` as soon as a file changes. On wasip1
only, doDiff now prints the hunks itself (unified.go) over the edit list of
buf's own diffmyers package, following GNU `diff -u`: 3 context lines,
hunks merged across at most 6 lines, deletions before insertions, and
"\ No newline at end of file". The header still goes through
tryModifyHeader. Other platforms keep calling `diff`.

Checked against GNU diff on 300 random edits: patch(1) applies every diff
to the exact target, and 240 are byte-identical to GNU's output; the rest
choose an equally minimal alignment among repeated lines.

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).
removeWhen: buf prints diffs without an external binary.

